// # c_emit Template-Based Emit — Phase C Spec
//
// Logline: Replace imperative `println("  " + lty + " " + name + " = " + rhs + ";")` in 11 c_emit_*.oo files with a typed-AST → C template pipeline, eliminating the 13 + 35 + 4 + 19 = 71 row "imperative emit" cluster by making init, order, prefix, dedup, and indent structurally impossible to get wrong.
//
// Setup: Phase A (audit/green/c_emit_refactor_design.oot:74-113) produced AstItem / AstTy / AstExpr / AstStmt and a type-check pass (catches 593 of 1,208 rows pre-emit). Phase B (parent:115-130) introduced EmitProgram as the per-build state container (typedefs, fn_protos, fn_bodies, cap_grants as Maps; 38 → 0 redef). This Phase C consumes the resolved AST and writes into EmitProgram via templates. Catalog: audit/green/master_blocked_catalog.oot (1,405 BLOCKED). The 256-line cap (FORMAT.oot:91) is a hard law. No source edits in this file; this is the durable design record. Note: the request's `c_emit_fn.oo:51` reference is a parameter-parse line; signature string concat is at c_emit_fn.oo:146 — both cited below.
//
// Beats:
//   §1  Goal
//   §2  Current pain (5 imperative-concat bugs, file:line)
//   §3  Phase C scope (in / out)
//   §4  Template model (AstNode → C template)
//   §5  Emit pipeline (7 steps: resolved AST → .c file)
//   §6  Migration path
//   §7  Acceptance criteria (5 measurable)
//   §8  Risks (5)
//
// Notes: This spec is sub-ordinate to the parent design at audit/green/c_emit_refactor_design.oot (Phase A + B + C). Phases A and B are already in (per parent:174-206); this spec covers only Phase C. Citation convention is file:line. Where a request-stage line reference is approximate, the verified line is cited and the discrepancy is noted in the Setup line. The 256-line cap (FORMAT.oot:91) applies to every .oot in this directory.

// ## §1. Goal
//
// Replace the imperative string-concat style in c_emit_call.oo, c_emit_call_ty.oo, c_emit_lower.oo, c_emit_ty.oo, c_emit_let.oo, c_emit_let_ext.oo, c_emit_match_let.oo, c_emit_deref.oo, c_emit_meta.oo, c_emit_preamble.oo (10 files / ~2,800 lines) with a small template layer that maps each AstItem / AstStmt / AstExpr to one C template. The C text is generated from a typed AST (Phase A) into a per-build EmitProgram (Phase B), then serialized by a single writer. The template layer is the only place that knows C syntax; the same templates are reusable by bc_emit and wasm_emit later. After Phase C, no emit decision is "did the developer remember the `OoRes_` prefix" — that prefix is in the template, not in the call site.

// ## §2. Current pain — bugs caused by imperative string concat
//
// | # | bug | file:line evidence | catalog row | count |
// |---|-----|--------------------|-------------|-------|
// | 1 | `let x = if ... { ... } else { ... };` emits decl with `={0}` literal C init (c_emit_let.oo:52) then runs the if via `__asgn__`; some paths skip decl entirely (c_emit_deref.oo:25 has no init in the EQ branch). The `={0}` is a C99 placeholder that fails to compile when the type is non-scalar (e.g. struct/union). | c_emit_let.oo:52 + c_emit_let.oo:245 + c_emit_deref.oo:25 | init_temps | 13 |
// | 2 | Declare-before-use broken: `__decl__` / `__formal__` ordering is checked at concat time. The 160-line IDENT dispatch in c_emit_lower.oo:97-256 emits C text in source-token order, so a use that precedes a decl in the source produces `undeclared` C. The 5-cell pack in c_emit_call.oo:47-140 compounds this by inlining pre/post cells. Fn signature string concat at c_emit_fn.oo:146 (`let mut sig = ret_ty + " " + c_fn_name`) carries the same source-order assumption. | c_emit_lower.oo:97-256 + c_emit_call.oo:47-140 + c_emit_fn.oo:146 | declarations | 35 |
// | 3 | `OoRes_` prefix missing in 4 known call sites. c_emit_result.oo:177-235 uses char_at probes (chars 0,2,3,4,7) to decide between `OoResI`, `OoResS`, `OoResF` (the 4 catalog rows) and forgets the `OoRes_` prefix in the OoResF and OoResS branches. c_emit_call_ty.oo:5-101 has 4 if-lists that re-derive the same names via string compare. | c_emit_result.oo:177-235 + c_emit_call_ty.oo:5-101 | result_cell | 4 |
// | 4 | Duplicate struct/union typedef. The per-file `#ifndef OO_TY_<name>` band-aid (c_emit_struct.oo:85-93) guards the typedef but NOT `OoRes_<name>` (c_emit_struct.oo:91) or `oo_retain_<name>` (c_emit_struct.oo:88). Two .oo files exporting same struct still produce two `oo_retain_X` fns and two `OoRes_X` typedefs. | c_emit_struct.oo:85-93 (band-aid) + c_emit_struct.oo:88, 91 (unguarded) | redef (residual) | ~6 |
// | 5 | Manual indent and newline: `println("  " + ...)` vs `println("    " + ...)` copy-pasted across c_emit_let.oo:89-148 (4-level nested if) and c_emit_match_let.oo:19-256 (match-let with per-arm indent). `;\n` vs `;\n}` is also manual. 19 catalog rows trace to indent or newline drift. | c_emit_let.oo:89-148 + c_emit_match_let.oo:19-256 | other lower | 19 |
// | 6 | Metamorphic preamble is a 4-style string-concat ladder (c_emit_meta.oo:135 + 137 + 141 + 148, 4 distinct decoy bodies) wrapped in a per-style `if`-ladder at c_emit_meta.oo:116-152. The 64-decoy cap and the 4-style identity are scattered across the concat sites; adding a 5th style means editing 5 separate println calls. | c_emit_meta.oo:116-152 (4-style ladder) + c_emit_meta.oo:135, 137, 141, 148 (per-style body) | metamorphic drift | 0 (R1 risk) |
//
// All 6 are structural. A template layer with named holes, an indent stack, and a single C-name registry per build makes each bug syntactically impossible.

// ## §3. Phase C scope
//
// In scope:
//   - Create c_template.oo: format with named holes, indent stack, newline policy.
//   - Create c_lower_expr.oo: match over AstExpr → C text (14 arms: ELitInt, ELitStr, ELitBool, EVar, EBinop, EUnop, ECall, EField, EArrow, EIndex, EMethod, EStruct, EIf, EMatch, EBlock, EClosure).
//   - Create c_lower_stmt.oo: match over AstStmt → C text (SLet, SLetMut, SAssign, SExpr, SWhile, SReturn, SEmpty).
//   - Create c_lower_ty.oo: AstTy → C name (TyInt, TyFloat, TyBool, TyStr, TyUnit, TyList, TyResult, TyName, TyCap, TyRef, TyRefMut).
//   - Create c_lower_item.oo: AstItem → C text (AstImport, AstType, AstFn, AstTrait, AstImpl, AstVerify).
//   - Wire c_program.oo (Phase B) to call lower_* in order; EmitProgram gains one mutator per field so lower_* cannot write to the wrong bucket.
//   - Add 1 C-name registry (Map<String, String>) for List kinds: replaces c_emit_ty.oo:46-144 5×5 ladder and c_emit_list_ty.oo:14-31 hardcodes.
//   - Add 1 free-fn table (Set<String>) for the 50+ names currently inlined in c_emit_call.oo:115-235 + c_emit_call_ty.oo:5-101.
//
// Out of scope:
//   - Phase A parser / type-check (already done; uses ast.oo + ty.oo from parent design:174-181).
//   - Phase B per-build state (already done; uses EmitProgram from parent design:183-189).
//   - Multi-TU builds (c_mangle_fn_name stays residual; c_program.oo is single-TU).
//   - path-A metamorphic decoys (R1: c_emit_meta.oo 4-style table preserved as a template variant, not re-derived; the 64-decoy cap stays in EmitProgram.cap_grants).
//   - SECRET/print guards (c_emit_secret*.oo stay orthogonal).
//   - 11 c_emit_*.oo files that are pure helpers (c_emit_skip_*, c_emit_helpers.oo, c_emit_env.oo, c_emit_args.oo) — stay; Phase C consumes them via lower_* callers.
//
// File count delta: +5 new (c_template.oo, c_lower_expr.oo, c_lower_stmt.oo, c_lower_ty.oo, c_lower_item.oo). -10 deleted (c_emit_call.oo, c_emit_call_ty.oo, c_emit_lower.oo, c_emit_ty.oo, c_emit_let.oo, c_emit_let_ext.oo, c_emit_let_ext_crt.oo, c_emit_match_let.oo, c_emit_deref.oo, c_emit_meta.oo, c_emit_preamble.oo). Net -5 files. Line count: ~1,200 new (templates + lowers) vs ~2,800 deleted. Net -1,600 lines.

// ## §4. Template model
//
// A template is a C string with named holes `{name}`. Phase C adds format() with hole substitution from a Ctx, not positional concat:
//
//   ctx: { indent: Int, env: TyEnv, res: &mut EmitProgram, tmp: Int }
//
// One template per AST node kind. Templates are data (String constants), not code. Examples:
//
//   | AstNode    | template                                                |
//   |------------|---------------------------------------------------------|
//   | SLet       | "{indent}{lty} {name} = {rhs};"                         |
//   | SLetMut    | "{indent}{lty} {name} = {rhs};"                         |
//   | SAssign    | "{indent}{lhs} = {rhs};"                                |
//   | SReturn    | "{indent}return {expr};"                                 |
//   | SWhile     | "{indent}while ({cond}) {{"                             |
//   | SExpr      | "{indent}{expr};"                                        |
//   | ELitInt    | "{value}"                                                |
//   | ECall      | "{callee}({args})"                                       |
//   | EField     | "{recv}.{field}"                                         |
//   | EArrow     | "{recv}->{field}"                                        |
//   | EIndex     | "oo_{kind}_get({base}, {idx})"                          |
//   | EStruct    | "(({cname}){{ {fields} }})"                              |
//   | AstType    | "typedef struct {cname} {{ {fields} }} {cname};"       |
//   | AstFn      | "{ret_ty} {cname}({params}) {{"                         |
//
// Each `lower_*` is a pure function: (ctx, ast) → C string. It does not println; it returns text. The caller (lower_stmt / lower_item) decides where to push it (EmitProgram.fn_bodies for body text, .typedefs for types, .fn_protos for protos). Newline and indent are owned by the format layer; the template contains literal `\n` and the layer respects ctx.indent. Prefix-typo bugs (the `OoRes_` problem in §2 #3) become impossible: lower_ty for TyResult always returns `OoRes_<elem_c_name>` — there is no other path. Hole-name typos (Risk §8 #4) are caught by binding holes to a typed record at compile time, not a Map<String, String>.

// ## §5. Emit pipeline (resolved AST → .c file)
//
// 7 steps, top to bottom. Steps 1-3 are Phase A+B; Phase C owns 4-6; step 7 is unchanged.
//
//   1. Parse.  ast.oo (Phase A) produces AstProgram: List<AstItem>. Errors here are tc errors, not C errors.
//   2. Type-check.  ty.oo (Phase A) produces TypedProgram: List<TypedItem>, with TyEnv carried in. 593 rows close pre-emit.
//   3. Resolve.  resolve.oo (Phase B) walks TypedProgram once, populates EmitProgram: { typedefs: Map, fn_protos: Map, fn_bodies: List, cap_grants: List, imports_h: Set }. Each typedef/fn goes in exactly once (38 → 0 redef).
//   4. Lower items.  lower_item.oo walks EmitProgram.items; for each AstType → push to .typedefs; for each AstFn → lower_signature → push to .fn_protos; for each AstImport → push to .imports_h. Pure text accumulation; no println.
//   5. Lower bodies.  for each fn body, lower_stmt.oo recurses over AstStmt; for each expression, lower_expr.oo recurses over AstExpr. Output text is appended to .fn_bodies with the fn's indent (0 for top-level, +1 per block). Names are resolved via TyEnv (no `char_at` probes, no `__ret_int__` env side-channel). Declare-before-use is enforced: TyEnv.declare(name, ty) runs before any nested lower_expr that could reference name.
//   6. Serialize.  c_program.oo walks EmitProgram in fixed order: imports_h → typedefs → fn_protos → globals (cap grants) → fn_bodies. Each map entry is one line; each list element is one block. Newlines are owned by the serializer, not the lowerer.
//   7. Write.  c_program.oo writes the serialized text to <build>/<name>.c; gcc compiles. The gcc driver in c_emit.oo:222-249 stays; Phase C replaces only the producer of the .c text, not the writer.

// ## §6. Migration path
//
// 1. Add c_template.oo + c_lower_ty.oo + golden test (one C construct per test). Gate: golden = 0 diff on `let x: Int = 5;`.
//   2. Add c_lower_expr.oo + c_lower_stmt.oo. Wire c_program.oo to call them. Run behind flag `OODAC_PHASE_C=1`; old c_emit_*.oo still runs in parallel. Gate: 3 known-green std/ files (std/io/print.oo, std/str/parse.oo, std/list/ops.oo) byte-identical .c output.
//   3. Add c_lower_item.oo for AstType + AstFn proto. Move typedefs + fn_protos to template layer. Gate: test_resolve_redef.oo still passes (Phase B invariants preserved); 0 `OoRes_` prefix misses (test_lower_ty_result.oo).
//   4. Cut over once/once_noarc mode to Phase C; keep all/once_arc on c_emit for one release as diff reference. Gate: build of std/io/print.oo is byte-identical OR diff is justified per-line.
//   5. Delete c_emit_call.oo, c_emit_call_ty.oo, c_emit_lower.oo, c_emit_ty.oo, c_emit_let.oo, c_emit_let_ext.oo, c_emit_let_ext_crt.oo, c_emit_match_let.oo, c_emit_deref.oo, c_emit_meta.oo, c_emit_preamble.oo. Update check_drive.oo:31 to drop the `extra_binds` string-hack (now a TyEnv field from Phase A's tc_import).
//   6. Run prove: audit/green/green_check.oo + audit/green/prove_runner.oo over all 22 audit siblings. Gate: library_status.oot BLOCKED drops below 200 (from 1,405).
//
// Each step is a single PR with its own gate. The build remains green between steps because c_emit_*.oo stays in the build until step 4. We can stop after step 3 if pressure is real: AST + lower_ty + lower_expr already in, full A+B+C value realized in std/.

// ## §7. Acceptance criteria (5 measurable)
//
//   1. **Golden diff = 0.** test_c_emit_template.oo covers 12 C constructs (let, fn, struct, while, if, match, call, method, arrow, field, index, struct-lit) and 3 known-green std/ files (std/io/print.oo, std/str/parse.oo, std/list/ops.oo). Each golden file is the current c_emit output. Phase C output must byte-equal it. Any diff is a bug.
//   2. **init_temps: 13 → 0.** template `{indent}{lty} {name} = {rhs};` always emits the init; the `={0}` literal placeholder (c_emit_let.oo:52) and the no-init bug (c_emit_deref.oo:25) become unreachable. Test: c_emit_let_init_required.oo asserts every SLet produces a non-empty rhs in the emitted C.
//   3. **declarations: 35 → 0.** lower_stmt.oo on SLet pushes to .fn_bodies AND TyEnv.declare(name) before any nested lower_expr runs. Source-order emission is replaced by declare-before-use ordering at the AST walk. Test: c_emit_decl_before_use.oo walks an SUse-before-SLet AST and asserts the let decl appears before the use in the emitted C text.
//   4. **result_cell: 4 → 0.** lower_ty(TyResult(t1, t2)) returns `OoRes_<c_name_of t1>` exactly; the 4 char_at probes in c_emit_result.oo:177-235 and the 4 if-lists in c_emit_call_ty.oo:5-101 are gone. Test: c_emit_ty_result_prefix.oo asserts every TyResult type lowers to a string starting with `OoRes_`.
//   5. **library_status.oot < 200 BLOCKED.** parent design doc (audit/green/c_emit_refactor_design.oot:270) sets this as the cross-phase target. Phase A closes 593, Phase B closes 38, Phase C closes 13 + 35 + 4 + 19 = 71; total = 702 closed; remaining < 200 requires A+B+C together. Phase C alone closes ≥ 71 rows (per parent design:202-206).

// ## §8. Risks (5)
//
//   1. **Pratt parser precedence drift.** parse_expr_bp (Phase A) precedence may differ from current c_emit_primary_c ladder on 1-2 constructs (notably `match` and `if`-as-expr). Mitigation: Phase A ships parse_expr_bp_diff.oo (parent design:228-231) diffing AST on 50 known-green std/ files; Phase C adds a second diff at the lower_expr layer so any lower-time precedence bug is caught before .c write.
//   2. **Free-name table drift.** the 50+ free fn names currently inlined in c_emit_call.oo:115-235 + c_emit_call_ty.oo:5-101 move to a Set<String>; any name we miss silently disappears from the C output. Mitigation: Phase A test test_tc_call_known_free_names.oo enumerates every name in c_is_res_s_call / c_is_slist_call / c_is_i64_call / c_is_str_call and asserts it still type-checks; Phase C adds test_lower_expr_free_names.oo that asserts every free name lower_expr emits matches a literal C string from a snapshot of c_emit_call_ty.oo:5-101.
//   3. **Indent stack overflow.** c_emit_match_let.oo:19-256 nests 4 levels of indent via `"  "` * n string concat. Phase C's indent stack (`ctx.indent = push(ctx.indent, 1)`) has no hard cap. Mitigation: lower_stmt.oo asserts ctx.indent < 32 per body (c_emit_let.oo:57 is the precedent hard cap); emit a tc warning at indent > 16, hard fail at indent > 32.
//   4. **Template hole name typos.** `{lhs}` vs `{lsh}` is a string-compare bug we are introducing by using holes. Mitigation: c_template.oo binds holes from a typed record (e.g. `LetHole { lty: String, name: String, rhs: String }`) at compile time; the template is a function `Fn(Holes) -> String`, not a string with `{name}` markers. format() takes `(template: Fn(Holes) -> String, holes: Holes)`, not `(template: String, holes: Map<String, String>)`. The hole set is closed per template; typo = compile error.
//   5. **Phase B invariant breach.** Phase C lowers into EmitProgram; if a lower_* call writes to the wrong field (e.g. lower_stmt writes a decl to .fn_protos), Phase B's per-program dedup silently mis-dedups. Mitigation: c_program.oo exposes EmitProgram as a typed record with one mutator per field (push_typedef, push_fn_proto, push_fn_body, push_cap_grant); lower_* cannot reach the underlying List/Map directly. Test: test_lower_item_dispatch.oo asserts each AstItem kind goes to its correct field across 50 fixtures.
